Name : Zeus Stats.

By   : Mike Henderson (Chaos Engine BBS)


Ok, here are the Docs for the Door.

The whole package could probably be a lot better, but since this is my first
go at programming a door for Zeus, it will have to do.

The door is one of these last callers type things, and will display mail
calls as well as BBS calls.

To install, just Unarc the whole directory into doors:



There are three Arexx routines.


Mailstats.rexx.

I call this from within GMS using

endSession="rx doors:stats/Mailstats.rexx %B %n %d %S"

This will log the mail call to the datafile.

The Template for Mailstats.rexx is...

Mailstats.rexx Baud Address Direction Name.

The same variables will probably do for other mailers, but i've not tested
it with them.


The next routine is..

BBSstats.rexx

Call this somewhere in your Postlogon.pl with.

Callscript 'doors:stats/bbsstats.rexx'

This will log the BBS user to the datafile.

There is a variable called 'loc' within this file, set this to '1' if you
dont want local calls logged.


The third routine is Stats.rexx which displays the actually information to
the BBS user.

Use..

Callscript 'doors:stats/stats.rexx' somewhere in the Postlogon.pl.



Ok, thats all there is to it. I've included a blank data file, but the next
version will create this itself.

I've released this earlier than expected due to the continual nagging of
Dave Naylor from FrostFree BBS.

Please feel free to Alter the Header & Footer files to suite your own BBS,
but remember that the Number of lines of these files are important, as is
the width if it is going to line up with the central data file.



DISCLAIMER...

I take no responsibilty if this collection of programs completely trashes
you harddisk or does any other harm to your system. This package is for Zeus
BBS systems, but could probably be altered to suite any other BBS package.




